Develop a Java program that includes a class responsible for handling student information. The class must contain the student's ID, name, and also a list of grades for the five subjects taken in the semester. 

Additionally, the class should provide methods to calculate the average grade of the student, and display an error message if no grades (or incomplete grades) are provided. 

Here's a simple piece of code. Identify the mistakes, debug it, and improve upon it:

```Java
public class Student {
    int studentId;
    String studentName;
    double grades[]; 

    public Student(int id, String name, double[] grades){
        this.studentId = id;
        this.studentName = name;
        this.grades = grades;
    }
    public double averageGrade(){
        double sum = 0;
        for(int i=0;i<grades.length;i++){
            sum+= grades[i];
            return sum/grades.length;
        }
    }
}
```
Validate your class by creating multiple student objects and test the grade average calculation. Beware of potential division by zero situations. There should be 2 paragraphs. Paragraphs and only paragraphs are separated with each other by two line breaks.

